# Prompts (`@lobechat/prompts`)

Full playbook: `packages/prompts/PROMPT_ENGINEERING.md`.

## Directory layout per prompt

```
promptfoo/<prompt-name>/
├── eval.yaml           # promptfoo config (providers, prompt ref, tests ref)
├── prompt.ts           # prompt definition (default export)
└── tests/basic-case.ts # TypeScript test cases (default export)
```

## Core conventions

- **English system prompts** — better cross-language and cross-model consistency. Use Chinese only for pure-Chinese tasks.
- **Be explicit about output shape** — `Output ONLY the translated text, no explanations`.
- **Use examples** to pin behavior (`"I got a promotion" → 🎉`).
- **Layer rules** with MUST > SHOULD > MAY.
- **Preserve technical terms** verbatim (`API_KEY_12345`, code identifiers, provider names).

## Tests

- Put test cases in `tests/basic-case.ts` (TypeScript, `export default` array) — not inline in `eval.yaml`.
- Cover at least 3–5 languages + edge cases (empty input, technical terms, mixed-language, unrelated context).
- Common assertion types: `llm-rubric`, `contains` / `contains-any`, `not-contains`, `javascript`, `regex`.

## Evaluation loop

```bash
pnpm promptfoo eval -c promptfoo/<prompt-name>/eval.yaml
```

Iterate: run → analyze failures → refine prompt → re-run. Expect 3–5 rounds to reach 100%. Adjust tests (not prompt) when expectations are unreasonable.
